// aug31c (fleet, minimized further by hand): the fused fold derived its
// firing bit from the ACC CARRY alone (`result_is_firing`, ba524ee8 #9)
// — the last body evaluation's STALE. Here slot 0 (v=1) consumes the
// fired init through its `_ => acc` arm, but slot 1 (v=2) takes the
// constant arm, so the final carry is stale and the kernel stayed
// quiet while FoldQ's per-slot rule (`any_trig`: any slot PRODUCTION
// triggers) fires. ba524ee8 matched the pre-dense consumption-chain
// node-walk; the organic-tags rework re-ruled the interp to per-slot
// productions (dense_delivery.md, the twochannel class) and the kernel
// was never revisited. Fix: the body evaluation's STALE folds into the
// slots word each iteration (`SlotFlags::fold_stale`); the carry stays
// an ADDITIONAL firing source (it alone covers the empty-source fold
// under a fired init); TAINT still rides only the carry (consumption
// decides — an acc-ignoring callback recovers).
// Interp [0:[0] 1:[0] 2:[0] 3:[0] 4:[0]]; JIT fired only [0:[0]].
{let x = array::iter([i64:1, i64:2, i64:3, i64:4]); let evens: Array<i64> = array::fold([i64:1, i64:2], [x], |acc, v| select v % i64:2 {i64:0 => [i64:0], _ => acc}); evens}
